  "term": "vegetative state",
  "definition": "In cognition, vegetative state is a neurocognitive status seen in people with severe brain damage in which physiologic functions such as sleep-wake cycles, autonomic control, and breathing continue, while awareness, including all cognitive function and emotion, is absent.",
